WEBVTT


WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.900
The Silver Reed YC6 Yarn Changer is

2
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:08.980
designed to be used for both
single and double bed knitting.

3
00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.180
In comparison, for Brother machines,

4
00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:16.020
there are separate color changers
for single and double bed.

5
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.380
Just so you don't get confused as I'm

6
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.340
recording this, I may use the term color
changer and yarn changer alternately.

7
00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.340
I mean the same thing.

8
00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:30.100
Start by tilting the bed
by using the ribber clamps.

9
00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.940
Even if you're going to be using the color
changer for single bed knitting,

10
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.220
you need to tilt the bed so
the device fits in place.

11
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.900
Once the bed is secure with the ribber

12
00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:46.500
clamps, make room for the color changer
by pushing the sponge bar to the right.

13
00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:49.620
It'll protrude 2 to 3 CM on the right

14
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:56.400
side, and it'll remain in this position
as long as the color changer is in place.

15
00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.700
Loosen the setting wheel until it stops.

16
00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.100
This is releasing the setting plate

17
00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:09.400
that will be inserted into the needle
bed where the sponge bar normally lives.

18
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.210
Insert that setting plate and wiggle
it around until it seats.

19
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.900
At the same time, push the color changer
towards the right until the edge

20
00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:25.400
of that yarn changer sits firmly
against the end of the bed.

21
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:33.040
Push the release button to align all
the holder buttons to the "O" position.

22
00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:41.140
When I got my color changer,
this holder was all the way out.

23
00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:46.570
I gently pulled it out a little more,
felt a click, and then released it.

24
00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.780
The spring brought it back into position.

25
00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:55.380
By pushing the release button,
it aligned that holder with the others.

26
00:01:55.410 --> 00:02:01.340
In this position,
all the holders are out of work. Again,

27
00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.260
because this color changer can be used

28
00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:09.170
in two ways, we need to align it into its
correct position for how we're knitting.

29
00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.780
For single bed knitting,

30
00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:19.960
loosen the change screw and push
the arm up, and then tighten the screw.

31
00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.730
For double bed knitting, loosen
the change screw and let the arm drop.

32
00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:31.100
Then tighten that screw again
to secure the changer arm.

33
00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:34.260
Next, we'll set up the tension mast.

34
00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.660
Snap the tension guide onto the yarn rod

35
00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:44.900
or the yarn mast and slide it down
to secure it so it doesn't twist around.

36
00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.380
Carefully pull up the tension spring

37
00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:52.280
of the tensioner assembly
and snap it into position.

38
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.180
Insert the yarn rod or that mast
into the front slot of the tensioner.

39
00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:10.780
It insert the lower end of the yarn rod or
mast into the slot in the needle bed

40
00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:15.140
and rotate it so it's
secure and doesn't twist.

41
00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:22.360
Next, exchange the knitter connecting
sinker plate with the yarn changer arm

42
00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:30.160
and you're ready to start
using your yarn changer.

